/-
  GPn7T.lean — generalized Petersen graphs GP(n,7), n ≥ 15: the colouring (tables and definitions).

  GP(n,7) = `GPk.gp n 7` (see GPPeriodic.lean): u_i = 2i, v_i = 2i+1; edges 3i: u_i u_{i+1}, 3i+1: u_i v_i,
  3i+2: v_i v_{i+7}.  Colouring: for n ≥ 31 a periodic part of period 8 (patterns P0..P7; block
  J < n - n mod 8 - 8 gets P_(J mod 8)) followed by a seam of length n mod 8 + 8 that depends on n mod 8;
  explicit colourings for 15 ≤ n < 31.  A pattern is [outer, spoke, inner] with colours 0..4.
  The tables were found by a SAT search on 2026-10-02 (search/gpsearch.py, search/gp7.json); this file was generated
  by search/gen_gpk.py.  The Lean proof does not depend on the search: all windows are checked by `decide`.
-/
